\section{DuckDB Extension Template}

\textbf{Status:} Production Ready \textbar{} \textbf{Version:} 2.0.0 \textbar{} \textbf{License:} MIT

A \textbf{comprehensive} template for building \href{https://duckdb.org}{DuckDB} extensions with \emph{modern C++ practices} and full CI/CD support.

\begin{quote}
\textbf{Important:} This template requires DuckDB v1.0+ and a C++17 compatible compiler. See \protect\hyperlink{requirements}{Requirements} for details.
\end{quote}

\subsection{Features}

\begin{itemize}
\tightlist
\item
  \textbf{Modern Build System}

  \begin{itemize}
  \tightlist
  \item
    CMake-based configuration
  \item
    Supports \texttt{vcpkg} and \texttt{conan}
  \item
    Cross-platform compatibility
  \end{itemize}
\item
  \textbf{Testing Infrastructure}

  \begin{itemize}
  \tightlist
  \item
    Unit tests with GoogleTest
  \item
    Integration tests with sqllogictest
  \item
    Coverage reports via \texttt{lcov}
  \end{itemize}
\item
  \textbf{CI/CD Pipeline}

  \begin{itemize}
  \tightlist
  \item
    GitHub Actions workflows
  \item
    Automatic releases
  \item
    Multi-platform builds (Linux, macOS, Windows)
  \end{itemize}
\end{itemize}

\subsection{Installation}

Install directly from the DuckDB CLI:

\begin{Shaded}
\begin{Highlighting}[]
\NormalTok{INSTALL extension\_name }\KeywordTok{FROM}\NormalTok{ community;}
\NormalTok{LOAD extension\_name;}
\end{Highlighting}
\end{Shaded}

Or build from source:

\begin{Shaded}
\begin{Highlighting}[]
\FunctionTok{git}\NormalTok{ clone https://github.com/user/extension.git}
\BuiltInTok{cd}\NormalTok{ extension}
\FunctionTok{make}\NormalTok{ release}
\FunctionTok{make}\NormalTok{ test}
\end{Highlighting}
\end{Shaded}

\subsection{Quick Start}

\begin{enumerate}
\def\labelenumi{\arabic{enumi}.}
\tightlist
\item
  \textbf{Clone} the repository
\item
  \textbf{Configure} your extension name in \texttt{CMakeLists.txt}
\item
  \textbf{Implement} your functions in \texttt{src/}
\item
  \textbf{Test} with \texttt{make\ test}
\item
  \textbf{Release} via GitHub Actions
\end{enumerate}

\subsection{API Reference}

\subsubsection{Scalar Functions}

The \texttt{my\_function} scalar function accepts a \texttt{VARCHAR} and returns a \texttt{BIGINT}:

\begin{Shaded}
\begin{Highlighting}[]
\CommentTok{{-}{-} Basic usage}
\KeywordTok{SELECT}\NormalTok{ my\_function(}\StringTok{\textquotesingle{}input\textquotesingle{}}\NormalTok{) }\KeywordTok{AS}\NormalTok{ result;}

\CommentTok{{-}{-} With table data}
\KeywordTok{SELECT} \KeywordTok{id}\NormalTok{, my\_function(name) }\KeywordTok{AS}\NormalTok{ processed}
\KeywordTok{FROM}\NormalTok{ my\_table}
\KeywordTok{WHERE}\NormalTok{ active }\OperatorTok{=} \KeywordTok{true}\NormalTok{;}
\end{Highlighting}
\end{Shaded}

\subsubsection{Table Functions}

Use \texttt{my\_table\_function} to generate rows:

\begin{Shaded}
\begin{Highlighting}[]
\KeywordTok{SELECT} \OperatorTok{*} \KeywordTok{FROM}\NormalTok{ my\_table\_function(}\DecValTok{10}\NormalTok{, }\StringTok{\textquotesingle{}config.json\textquotesingle{}}\NormalTok{);}
\end{Highlighting}
\end{Shaded}

\subsection{Configuration}

Configure via DuckDB settings:

\begin{Shaded}
\begin{Highlighting}[]
\KeywordTok{SET}\NormalTok{ extension\_option }\OperatorTok{=} \StringTok{\textquotesingle{}value\textquotesingle{}}\NormalTok{;}
\KeywordTok{SET}\NormalTok{ extension\_debug }\OperatorTok{=} \KeywordTok{true}\NormalTok{;}
\end{Highlighting}
\end{Shaded}

